When creating a new `Context(context)`, it doesn't pass the `autoescape` attribute from the engine (`self.autoescape`). So even if the engine is created with `autoescape=False`, the Context will still use the default `autoescape=True`.

The fix should be:
```python
return t.render(Context(context, autoescape=self.autoescape))
```

